<concept id="_Toc235450417" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Admonitions</title>
   <abstract>This section covers Admonitions — paragraph-level notices that give safety-related,
      advisory, or supplementary information structural separation from the surrounding body content
      — and five scenarios: a standard named admonition, consecutive admonitions, an image placed
      inside an admonition, an admonition inside a table cell, and a bold inline label pattern. The
      converter maps each recognized admonition style directly to <codeph>&lt;note
         type="[type]"&gt;</codeph>; for bold inline labels, content pattern recognition reads the
      opening text, removes the label, and maps the remaining content to the matching
      type.</abstract>
